back ('who closed what, when'), and README documents the repair as a safe operator action on a live board.", "created_at": "2026-10-23T11:26:21Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-23T21:36:07Z", "created_by": null, "acceptance_criteria": "1) An event appended while the repair runs must survive it: start `boardctl normalize-board --repair-events --apply` on a 60,000-event fixture with descending ids, then run `boardctl event --type audit --tick 999 --detail-text PROBE-EV-1 --no-tick-write` while it is running; after the apply exits, `grep -c PROBE-EV-1 events.jsonl` must print 1 (today it prints 0). 2) events.jsonl must be replaced atomically: kill -9 the process mid-rewrite and `grep -c` of a seeded marker in events.jsonl must print the same count as before the run, i.e. the previous file is still intact (not truncated). 3) internal/board/iddupe.go's DedupeByID must either take the same write guard around its read-then-atomicRewrite window or carry a comment stating why it is exempt: `sed -n '/func.*DedupeByID/,/^}/p' internal/board/iddupe.go` prints the guard call or the exemption comment. 4) A regression test interleaving an append with the repair must exit 1 before the fix and exit 0 after it: `go test ./internal/board -run Concurrent`. 5) Full suite exits 0: `go test ./...` expected exit code 0.", "capability_tags": [], "complexity": 3, "depends_on": [], "foreman_note": "Worker commit c742b964 was cherry-picked as ef1fcd6 on main and pushed. Verified gofmt, build, vet, focused Concurrent test, full go test -count=1 ./..., git diff --check, GitReins guard PASS, GitReins Tier 2 COMPLETE, and CI green.", "commit_hash": "ef1fcd660883d73aa327f1f96b0943645dd4ded3", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worker_summary": "RepairEvents and DedupeByID now hold the board write guard across read/classify/plan/rewrite; RepairEvents uses atomicRewrite; concurrent append regression and full Go suite pass. GitReins PASS at .gitreins/history/2026-10-23/fd61a183/verdict.json. ch:t