+ {"id": "DF-BOARDCTL-49", "title": "normalize-board --repair-events --apply drops EVENTS appended while it runs (5/5 attempts on both the released v0.1.11 and HEAD) and rewrites events.jsonl in place instead of atomically; dedupe-board's DedupeByID has the same unlocked read-then-rewrite shape", "status": "complete", "priority": "P2", "reasoning": "Dogfood run 25 (tick boardctl-dogfood-2026-10-23-10-52-34), second delivery. Same root cause as DF-BOARDCTL-48 on the events side.\n\nPROBE (/tmp/df1023/repro_events3.sh): events.jsonl seeded with 60,000 events carrying descending ids (so the repair has work); `normalize-board --repair-events --apply` started, then after 0.10s `event --type audit --tick 999 --detail-text PROBE-EV-<n> --no-tick-write` appended (rc=0, 'event id N appended'). Final file read back: the probe detail is ABSENT in 5/5 attempts on the HEAD build and 5/5 on the released v0.1.11 binary (apply rc=0 each time, 0.52-0.73s wall). A successful append that is not in the final file is an overwritten write; nothing reports it.\n\nMECHANISM: internal/board/repair_events.go RepairEvents(false) parses and renumbers every event before the guard, then acquires the write guard only around `os.WriteFile(b.eventsPath, out, 0o644)` (repair_events.go:209-214). The rewrite bytes come from the pre-append snapshot, so any event appended in between is discarded. Two aggravators: (a) that write is a plain os.WriteFile, not atomicRewrite(tmp+rename) as normalize-board uses, so a crash mid-write can truncate the whole event trail; (b) dedupe-board's DedupeByID calls atomicRewrite at internal/board/iddupe.go:234 with the read and planning above it (iddupe.go:107-236) and NO write guard anywhere in that function — the only guard in the file is in CloseIDDupeLine (iddupe.go:329). Same shape, not probed here because cmd/dedupe-board is a one-shot source-only tool; listed so the fix covers it in one pass.\n\nContext for severity: events.jsonl is the audit trail the fleet reads back ('who closed what, when'), and README documents the repair as a safe operator action on a live board.", "created_at": "2026-10-23T11:26:21Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-23T21:36:07Z", "created_by": null, "acceptance_criteria": "1) An event appended while the repair runs must survive it: start `boardctl normalize-board --repair-events --apply` on a 60,000-event fixture with descending ids, then run `boardctl event --type audit --tick 999 --detail-text PROBE-EV-1 --no-tick-write` while it is running; after the apply exits, `grep -c PROBE-EV-1 events.jsonl` must print 1 (today it prints 0). 2) events.jsonl must be replaced atomically: kill -9 the process mid-rewrite and `grep -c` of a seeded marker in events.jsonl must print the same count as before the run, i.e. the previous file is still intact (not truncated). 3) internal/board/iddupe.go's DedupeByID must either take the same write guard around its read-then-atomicRewrite window or carry a comment stating why it is exempt: `sed -n '/func.*DedupeByID/,/^}/p' internal/board/iddupe.go` prints the guard call or the exemption comment. 4) A regression test interleaving an append with the repair must exit 1 before the fix and exit 0 after it: `go test ./internal/board -run Concurrent`. 5) Full suite exits 0: `go test ./...` expected exit code 0.", "capability_tags": [], "complexity": 3, "depends_on": [], "foreman_note": "Worker commit c742b964 was cherry-picked as ef1fcd6 on main and pushed. Verified gofmt, build, vet, focused Concurrent test, full go test -count=1 ./..., git diff --check, GitReins guard PASS, GitReins Tier 2 COMPLETE, and CI green.", "commit_hash": "ef1fcd660883d73aa327f1f96b0943645dd4ded3", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worker_summary": "RepairEvents and DedupeByID now hold the board write guard across read/classify/plan/rewrite; RepairEvents uses atomicRewrite; concurrent append regression and full Go suite pass. GitReins PASS at .gitreins/history/2026-10-23/fd61a183/verdict.json. ch: